v3.5.0
fixed result pinning: retries never reconnected, so a stale connection
  flag failed every attempt against a healthy IPFS daemon
one failed pin/ls no longer disables pinning node-wide
serialised IPFS restarts across network threads (lock + 60s cooldown),
  which stops one thread's restart from breaking the others' calls
results that fail to pin are queued on disk and retried after an IPFS
  outage or a node restart, instead of being lost with the process
CAS endpoints are read from CasKeyStore rather than the registry, which
  no longer forwards them (requires a registry exposing keyStore())
3s RPC connect timeout, replacing 120s applied to both phases
HTTP sessions are closed when a network iteration ends
the shared task slot is acquired atomically, so two networks can no
  longer hold it at once or clear each other's ownership

